                        {
                            "id": "IC_kwDOAPphoM8AAAABpTRwGg",
                            "author": {
                                "__typename": "User",
                                "login": "barrettruth"
                            },
                            "body": "Actually, should we not at least have a test with symlinked ssh configs? Should we also not have a recursive depth guard? Is this impossible?\r\n\r\nWould really like to not introduce an infinite recursion on _parsing ssh configs_, of all things.",
                            "createdAt": "2026-11-21T17:39:20Z",
                            "viewerDidAuthor": false,
                            "viewerCanUpdate": false
                        },
                        {
                            "id": "IC_kwDOAPphoM8AAAABpZqdNQ",
                            "author": {
                                "__typename": "User",
                                "login": "ishianecho"
                            },
                            "body": "Seems symlinked configs are fine, the man page says \"Files without absolute paths are assumed to be in ~/.ssh if included in a user configuration file\". (Also added a test for this)\r\n\r\nAnyway, seems the failed tests have nothing to do with my changes.",
